    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but what about the people who argue that proximity to transit is the real equity issue? like, if we just give houses to low income people in the outskirts where there's no bus or train, aren't we just trapping them in a cycle of poverty? wouldn't prioritizing transit-adjacent housing be a more effective way to actually create equity than just looking at income levels alone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
